Keep compiled Vulkan pipelines across launches (VkPipelineCache)

vkCreateComputePipelines was passed VK_NULL_HANDLE, so every launch
recompiled each of the ~49 compute pipelines on first use; only a
per-process map kept them. This creates one VkPipelineCache at device
creation and passes it to every pipeline.

The cache is persisted only when the host names a file in
SPEKTRAFILM_VULKAN_PIPELINE_CACHE (the Android app puts it in cacheDir with
the app's version code in the name). The file carries a header of our own:
magic, device name, vendor and device id, driver version and
pipelineCacheUUID, plus the payload's length and FNV-1a hash. Anything that
does not match this device and driver exactly, or is short, oversized
(> 64 MiB) or corrupt, is ignored and the cache starts empty; a driver that
rejects the data gets an empty cache, and one that rejects that runs with
none, as before. It is written, to a temporary file then renamed, from
trim_pool(0) (the app trims when it goes to the background) and from the
destructor, and only when a pipeline was compiled since the last save.

Output: unchanged by construction. A pipeline cache only returns what the
driver compiled from the same SPIR-V, layout and specialisation constant;
nothing a shader computes depends on it. With the variable unset (desktop,
parity harness) the cache lives in memory for the process only.

